  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 318 AM EDT Saturday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3: Global guidance shows a large spread in potential \nsolutions associated with development/magnitude of mid/upper lvl \ntrof acrs the NE CONUS for this upcoming week. ECMWF/UKMET and ICON \nshow a deepening and closing off 700-500mb circulation acrs the NE \nCONUS/Mid Atlantic States Tues/Weds time frame, while GFS/CMC are \nless robust with closing system off and more progressive with \nmid/upper lvl trof lifting acrs the NE CONUS. The ECMWF/UKMET and \nICON solution would need to be watched closely for potential \nflooding, especially with slow moving showers/embedded thunder \nassociated with being directly under the closed low pres. Given the \nlarge ridge/trof amplification expected acrs the CONUS this upcoming \nweek, this solution has the potential to happen, as does a faster \nwith minimal impact scenario advertised by the GFS/CMC. A couple \nfactors could limit heavy rain potential, such as better instability \nis located to our south and closing mid/upper lvl circulation is \nassociated with northern stream energy with pw values only around 1 \nSTD above normal. We will continue to monitor later guidance \npackages and look for a trend in the potential outcomes. For now WPC \nhas 60 to 90% Tues/Weds with values tapering off to 30-40% by late \nweek. Highs generally at or slightly below normal, due to \nclouds/precip, but lows at or slightly above normal. Highs mainly \n70s to near 80 and lows upper 50s to mid 60s for Tues thru Fri.",
